According to Article 90, a qualified alert issued by the scientific panel must be **duly reasoned and must indicate at least**:

- **(a)** the point of contact of the provider of the general‑purpose AI model with the systemic risk concerned;  
- **(b)** a description of the relevant facts and the reasons for the alert by the scientific panel;  
- **(c)** any other information that the scientific panel considers relevant, including, where appropriate, information gathered on its own initiative.  

References: [Article 90](#chunk-1)
